<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of Documents</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shangshu, Classic of History, Shujing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of Documents (Shangshu) is one of the Five Classics of Chinese literature, a collection of speeches, proclamations and records attributed to the legendary sage kings and to rulers and ministers of the Xia, Shang and Western Zhou. Its oldest chapters, probably composed in the Western Zhou, set out the doctrine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandate-of-heaven">Mandate of Heaven</a>. Many chapters of the transmitted text were later shown to be forgeries of the fourth century CE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/book-of-documents.jpg" alt="Book of Documents" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guwen_Shangshu_TNM.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
